<!--
   QML card deck style "Blacklight 4c".

   A four colour deck under black light: the geometry (rank glyphs and suit
   symbols including their transformations) is taken over 1:1 from
   data/gfx/qml/cards/default4c - so rank heights and layout stay exactly those
   of the model. New are the colours and the glow.

   The colours are the inverted default4c colours, pulled towards neon:
     diamonds blue  #0039ff -> amber   #FFC400
     hearts   red   #d40000 -> cyan    #00EFFF
     spades   black #1a1a1a -> white   #F2F0FF
     clubs    green #267126 -> magenta #FF4DE8
   The card face is accordingly almost black with a violet tinge.

   QtSvg does not know filters (feGaussianBlur), so the glow is built from seven
   ever wider, ever weaker outlines below the fill. The faint neon edge of the
   card lifts the dark card off the dark table.

   Differing from default4c the rank glyph sits 7 units higher: there, rank (ink
   y 26..94) and suit symbol (y 97..149) are only 3 units apart, which the glow
   closes up. Now it is 10 units, and the set has 19 units of margin at the top
   as well as at the bottom.

   Generated with generate_blacklight_deck.py.

   Engine index -> card (see CardImage.qml):
     Suit = floor(index / 13): 0-12 diamonds(♦), 13-25 hearts(♥), 26-38 spades(♠), 39-51 clubs(♣)
     Rank = index % 13:        0=2, 1=3, … 8=10, 9=jack, 10=queen, 11=king, 12=ace
-->
<PokerTH>
  <CardDeck>
     <StyleDescription value="Blacklight 4c QML card deck" /><!-- Shown in the style selection -->
     <StyleMaintainerName value="PokerTH Development Team" />
     <StyleMaintainerEMail value="webmaster@pokerth.net" />
     <StyleCreateDate value="29.08.2026" />
     <PokerTHStyleFileVersion value="2" /><!-- Matches the version supported by the widget client -->
     <Preview value="preview.png" /><!-- Preview image (landscape only - no portrait needed) -->
     <BigIndexesActionBottom value="0" /><!-- Action labels not necessarily at the bottom -->
  </CardDeck>
</PokerTH>
